WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.738
Welcome back to your Danish citizenship exam companion.

2
00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:09.072
This is Chapter Six, Episode Six: immigration to Denmark through the ages.

3
00:00:09.622 --> 00:00:13.209
The Danish population is relatively homogeneous.

4
00:00:13.159 --> 00:00:17.297
That means most have the same language, culture and history.

5
00:00:17.297 --> 00:00:22.842
Even so, people from other countries have settled permanently in the country through the ages.

6
00:00:23.392 --> 00:00:30.079
They have come, among other reasons, as refugees, to work, or because they have married a Dane.

7
00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:38.367
This is many hundreds of years of immigration, which has put a certain mark on the Danish population, the Danish language and Danish culture.

8
00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:43.579
Immigration to Denmark has, however, been by far the biggest in recent times.

9
00:00:43.579 --> 00:01:04.188
Especially over the last decades, the number of immigrants and descendants of immigrants in Denmark has risen markedly: from about 150,000 in 1980 to one million in 2025, corresponding to 16.7 percent of Denmark's total population of six million, in other words roughly one in six.

10
00:01:04.738 --> 00:01:09.213
The Jews are an example of a minority that has been in Denmark for a long time.

11
00:01:09.163 --> 00:01:14.063
The first Jews came to Denmark in the 1600s at the invitation of the king.

12
00:01:14.063 --> 00:01:24.213
The Jews got a mixed reception and existence, and to get a residence permit they had to pay a large sum of money and submit to stricter legislation than the rest of the population.

13
00:01:24.213 --> 00:01:30.226
At the end of the 1700s, about 1,600 Jews lived in Copenhagen.

14
00:01:30.226 --> 00:01:42.063
The Jews gradually got more rights, and with the so-called Jewish Letter of Freedom, the "Jødiske Frihedsbrev", in 1814, the Jews were almost made equal with other Danes.

15
00:01:42.063 --> 00:01:48.613
At the beginning of the 1900s, a further approximately 3,000 Jews arrived in Denmark.

16
00:01:48.613 --> 00:01:51.942
They were fleeing poverty and persecution in Russia.

17
00:01:52.492 --> 00:01:57.680
In time the Jews became an accepted and well-integrated part of Danish society.

18
00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:08.680
Among other things, that is why by far most Danish Jews were helped to Sweden by Danish fellow citizens in 1943 during Nazi Germany's occupation of Denmark.

19
00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:15.120
Thereby they avoided the same extensive genocide as the Jews in the war's other German-controlled areas.

20
00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:21.582
In the time around the Second World War, it was especially war refugees who came to Denmark.

21
00:02:21.532 --> 00:02:31.722
The biggest group was the just under 240,000 war refugees from Germany, who came at the end of or right after the occupation, in 1945.

22
00:02:32.272 --> 00:02:42.547
In addition, around 23,000 war refugees came especially from the Soviet Union and the Baltic countries, Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania.

23
00:02:42.497 --> 00:02:49.476
At the end of the 1940s, the vast majority of these refugees had however returned to their home countries.

24
00:02:50.026 --> 00:02:59.238
In the first decades after the Second World War, it was first and foremost refugees from the East European countries who came to Denmark.

25
00:02:59.188 --> 00:03:18.246
Hungarian refugees came as a result of the uprising in Hungary in 1956, Czechoslovaks who fled during the Soviet invasion of Czechoslovakia in 1968, and Polish Jews who were forced to leave Poland because of an antisemitic wave in the country in 1968 to 69.

26
00:03:18.796 --> 00:03:27.696
Immigration in the 1960s was however in particular marked by guest workers from especially Turkey, Pakistan and the former Yugoslavia.

27
00:03:27.646 --> 00:03:31.632
They met a great need for foreign labour on the Danish labour market.

28
00:03:32.182 --> 00:03:37.669
A large part settled permanently in Denmark and later got their families to the country.

29
00:03:37.619 --> 00:03:43.794
That was namely still possible despite the stop for immigration that was introduced in 1973.

30
00:03:44.344 --> 00:03:51.294
In the 1970s, 1980s and 1990s, refugees again came to Denmark.

31
00:03:51.244 --> 00:04:01.319
These were not least refugees from the war between Iraq and Iran, 1980 to 88, and the civil war in Yugoslavia, 1991 to 95.

32
00:04:01.319 --> 00:04:14.028
In addition, refugees also came from, among other places, Vietnam, Sri Lanka, Somalia, and Palestinian refugees, who especially fled the civil war in Lebanon.

33
00:04:14.578 --> 00:04:24.240
Between 2000 and 2020, people especially from Afghanistan, the Middle East and Africa arrived, fleeing war and poverty.

34
00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:35.940
The number of asylum seekers who came to Europe and Denmark reached a peak during the so-called refugee crisis, where in total 21,000 sought asylum in Denmark in 2015.

35
00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.222
The biggest group had fled the civil war in Syria.

36
00:04:39.772 --> 00:04:45.584
In addition, in the same period many more foreigners have also come to Denmark to work.

37
00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:50.484
They have come from all over the world, but the majority from other EU countries.

38
00:04:50.484 --> 00:05:00.559
The number of immigrants and descendants from other EU countries has risen from 116,000 in 2000 to 318,000 in 2026.

39
00:05:00.559 --> 00:05:15.747
EU citizens have the right to freely work in other EU countries, and the majority of the increase can be attributed to the EU's enlargements in 2004, 2007 and 2013 with a total of 11 East European countries.

40
00:05:15.747 --> 00:05:24.792
These have meant that many East Europeans have moved to Western Europe, including Denmark, where wages are generally higher and living conditions better.

41
00:05:25.342 --> 00:05:32.729
Since Russia's invasion of Ukraine in February 2022, a large number of Ukrainians have arrived in Denmark.

42
00:05:32.679 --> 00:05:39.906
As of the first of January 2026, 44,000 displaced persons from Ukraine live in Denmark.

43
00:05:40.456 --> 00:05:46.393
Turkey, with 68,000, is the country most immigrants and descendants originate from.

44
00:05:46.343 --> 00:05:56.043
The ten countries that most immigrants and descendants in Denmark originate from are, in January 2026, thus Turkey, 68,000.

45
00:05:56.043 --> 00:05:58.481
Ukraine, 59,000.

46
00:05:58.481 --> 00:06:01.068
Poland, 57,000.

47
00:06:01.068 --> 00:06:03.756
Romania, 47,000.

48
00:06:03.756 --> 00:06:06.368
Syria, 46,000.

49
00:06:06.368 --> 00:06:08.768
Germany, 45,000.

50
00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:11.131
Iraq, 35,000.

51
00:06:11.131 --> 00:06:13.768
Pakistan, 29,000.

52
00:06:13.768 --> 00:06:16.143
Iran, 29,000.

53
00:06:16.143 --> 00:06:18.743
And Lebanon, 28,000.

54
00:06:18.743 --> 00:06:34.572
Of these, Poland, with 57,000, is the biggest origin country within the EU, ahead of Romania and Germany; Turkey, Ukraine, Syria, Iraq, Pakistan, Iran and Lebanon are not EU countries.

55
00:06:35.122 --> 00:06:37.522
Here is your recap for Episode Six.

56
00:06:37.472 --> 00:06:48.259
Immigrants and descendants grew from about 150,000 in 1980 to one million in 2025, which is 16.7 percent of six million.

57
00:06:48.259 --> 00:06:59.384
The first Jews came in the 1600s at the king's invitation; the Jewish Letter of Freedom was in 1814; about 3,000 Jews came in the early 1900s from Russia.

58
00:06:59.384 --> 00:07:03.284
Most Danish Jews were helped to Sweden in 1943.

59
00:07:03.284 --> 00:07:08.684
Almost 240,000 war refugees came from Germany in 1945.

60
00:07:08.684 --> 00:07:17.972
Hungarian refugees came after 1956, Czechoslovaks in 1968, and Polish Jews in 1968 to 69.

61
00:07:17.972 --> 00:07:27.147
Guest workers in the 1960s came from Turkey, Pakistan and the former Yugoslavia; the immigration stop was in 1973.

62
00:07:27.147 --> 00:07:34.422
In the refugee crisis, 21,000 sought asylum in 2015, mostly from Syria.

63
00:07:34.422 --> 00:07:48.109
EU immigrants and descendants grew from 116,000 in 2000 to 318,000 in 2026, after EU enlargements in 2004, 2007 and 2013.

64
00:07:48.109 --> 00:07:54.147
44,000 displaced Ukrainians lived in Denmark on the first of January 2026.

65
00:07:54.147 --> 00:08:05.934
The biggest origin countries in 2026 are Turkey, Ukraine, Poland, Romania, Syria, Germany, Iraq, Pakistan, Iran and Lebanon.

66
00:08:06.484 --> 00:08:09.084
Now it is time for your exam practice.

67
00:08:09.034 --> 00:08:13.946
These are real questions from past Danish citizenship exams on what you just heard.

68
00:08:13.946 --> 00:08:21.432
For each one, I will read the question and the choices, then pause so you can pick your answer, and then I will give you the correct answer.

69
00:08:21.982 --> 00:08:23.232
Question 1.

70
00:08:23.182 --> 00:08:30.519
Which group of citizens was helped, in their thousands, to flee from Denmark to Sweden in October 1943?

71
00:08:30.519 --> 00:08:32.919
Option A: Danish communists.

72
00:08:32.919 --> 00:08:35.482
Option B: Danish soldiers.

73
00:08:35.482 --> 00:08:37.914
Option C: Danish Jews.
[DA] Hvilken gruppe borgere blev i tusindtal hjulpet med at flygte fra Danmark til Sverige i oktober 1943?  A: Danske kommunister  |  B: Danske soldater  |  C: Danske jøder

74
00:08:44.464 --> 00:08:47.039
The answer is C: Danish Jews.

75
00:08:46.989 --> 00:08:51.396
It appeared in the November 2020 and November 2022 exams.
[DA] ✔ C: Danske jøder

76
00:08:51.946 --> 00:08:53.196
Question 2.

77
00:08:53.146 --> 00:08:58.496
From which of the following countries did the most immigrants come to Denmark in the 1960s?

78
00:08:58.496 --> 00:09:00.458
Option A: Hungary.

79
00:09:00.458 --> 00:09:02.333
Option B: Turkey.

80
00:09:02.333 --> 00:09:04.542
Option C: Vietnam.
[DA] Fra hvilket af følgende lande kom der flest indvandrere til Danmark i 1960’erne?  A: Ungarn  |  B: Tyrkiet  |  C: Vietnam

81
00:09:11.092 --> 00:09:13.292
The answer is B: Turkey.

82
00:09:13.242 --> 00:09:15.936
It appeared in the November 2020 exam.
[DA] ✔ B: Tyrkiet

83
00:09:16.486 --> 00:09:17.824
Question 3.

84
00:09:17.774 --> 00:09:24.749
From which country did over 200,000 war refugees come to Denmark in connection with the Second World War?

85
00:09:24.749 --> 00:09:26.599
Option A: France.

86
00:09:26.599 --> 00:09:28.586
Option B: Germany.

87
00:09:28.586 --> 00:09:30.138
Option C: Russia.
[DA] Fra hvilket land kom der over 200.000 krigsflygtninge til Danmark i forbindelse med 2. Verdenskrig?  A: Frankrig  |  B: Tyskland  |  C: Rusland

88
00:09:36.688 --> 00:09:38.951
The answer is B: Germany.

89
00:09:38.901 --> 00:09:41.796
It appeared in the November 2021 exam.
[DA] ✔ B: Tyskland

90
00:09:42.346 --> 00:09:43.646
Question 4.

91
00:09:43.596 --> 00:09:48.984
Which of the following countries do the most immigrants and descendants in Denmark originate from?

92
00:09:48.984 --> 00:09:51.246
Option A: Pakistan.

93
00:09:51.246 --> 00:09:53.059
Option B: Iran.

94
00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:55.086
Option C: Turkey.
[DA] Hvilket af følgende lande har flest indvandrere og efterkommere i Danmark oprindelse i?  A: Pakistan  |  B: Iran  |  C: Tyrkiet

95
00:10:01.636 --> 00:10:03.861
The answer is C: Turkey.

96
00:10:03.811 --> 00:10:06.600
It appeared in the June 2022 exam.
[DA] ✔ C: Tyrkiet

97
00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:08.613
Question 5.

98
00:10:08.563 --> 00:10:13.413
Which EU country do the most immigrants and descendants in Denmark originate from?

99
00:10:13.413 --> 00:10:15.300
Option A: Spain.

100
00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:17.213
Option B: Poland.

101
00:10:17.213 --> 00:10:19.266
Option C: France.
[DA] Hvilket EU-land har flest indvandrere og efterkommere i Danmark oprindelse i?  A: Spanien  |  B: Polen  |  C: Frankrig

102
00:10:25.816 --> 00:10:27.979
The answer is B: Poland.

103
00:10:27.929 --> 00:10:32.100
It appeared in the May 2023 and May 2025 exams.
[DA] ✔ B: Polen

104
00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.088
Question 6.

105
00:10:34.038 --> 00:10:39.625
From which country did especially many asylum seekers come to Denmark in 2015?

106
00:10:39.625 --> 00:10:41.613
Option A: Syria.

107
00:10:41.613 --> 00:10:43.425
Option B: Iran.

108
00:10:43.425 --> 00:10:45.534
Option C: Ukraine.
[DA] Fra hvilket land kom der særligt mange asylansøgere til Danmark i 2015?  A: Syrien  |  B: Iran  |  C: Ukraine

109
00:10:52.084 --> 00:10:54.147
The answer is A: Syria.

110
00:10:54.097 --> 00:10:57.048
It appeared in the November 2023 exam.
[DA] ✔ A: Syrien

111
00:10:57.598 --> 00:10:59.361
That's the end of this part.

112
00:10:59.311 --> 00:11:00.378
Well done.

